---
title: The Keeper of Gullwing Point
author: Emaki demo
start: arrival
title_image: bg/cliff_road_dusk.svg
---

# ── Characters ──────────────────────────────────────────────
define mira "Mira" color=#e8b04b
define ren "Ren" color=#8fc1e3
define radio "Radio" color=#9fd8a8

# ── Backgrounds ─────────────────────────────────────────────
image cliff_road = "bg/cliff_road_dusk.svg"
image kitchen = "bg/kitchen_night.svg"
image lamp_room = "bg/lamp_room_night.svg"
image shore_dawn = "bg/shore_dawn.svg"

# ── Mira's expressions ──────────────────────────────────────
image mira neutral = "sprites/mira_neutral.svg"
image mira smile = "sprites/mira_smile.svg"
image mira stern = "sprites/mira_stern.svg"
image mira sad = "sprites/mira_sad.svg"

# ── Sound (CC0, see assets/audio/CREDITS.md) ────────────────
audio theme = "audio/theme_forget_me_not.mp3" music "Forget Me Not"
audio storm = "audio/storm_rain.mp3" music "The Storm"
audio shore = "audio/shore_waves.mp3" music "Waves at Dawn"
audio thunder = "audio/thunder.mp3"
audio crank = "audio/crank.mp3"

# ── Story state ─────────────────────────────────────────────
var trust = 0
var read_letter = false
var lamp_fixed = false
var boat_safe = false

# ── Achievements (one per ending; Steam uses the same ids) ──
achievement two_keepers "Two Keepers"
achievement light_holds "The Light Holds"
achievement rough_water "Rough Water"

# ── Scenes to replay from Extras ────────────────────────────
replay kitchen_talk "A Talk in the Kitchen" image kitchen
replay lamp_room_trouble "Trouble in the Lamp Room" image lamp_room

label arrival:
  scene cliff_road with fade
  play music theme fade 2
  "The bus left me where the road gave up, a mile short of the lighthouse."
  "Gullwing Point. Forty years of logbooks, one keeper, and as of tonight, one relief assistant."
  "Me."
  show mira neutral at center with dissolve
  "She's waiting at the gate in an oilskin coat, as if she'd known to the minute when I'd arrive."
  mira: You're Ren.
  ren: That's me. Relief assistant, as of—
  mira: You're early. *Nobody's* ever early.

  menu:
    "The driver wanted to be home before the storm.":
      mira: Smart man. Smarter than most who come up this road.
    "I wanted to see the light come on.":
      set trust += 1
      mira smile: Did you now.
      mira: Then you'd better not miss it.

  mira neutral: Come on. Kettle's been on since noon.
  jump kitchen_talk

label kitchen_talk:
  scene kitchen with dissolve
  show mira neutral at right with dissolve
  "Her kitchen smells of coal tar and tea that has been stewing for hours."
  "There's a letter on the table. Sealed, addressed in her handwriting to the Lighthouse Board."
  mira: I'll check the barometer. Don't touch anything that ticks.
  hide mira with dissolve

  menu:
    "Read the letter.":
      set read_letter = true
      "I shouldn't. I do anyway. The wax is old and gives too easily."
      "It's short. She's resigning, effective the end of the month."
      "\"The Point needs someone who isn't tired,\" it says. \"I am tired.\""
    "Leave it alone.":
      set trust += 1
      "Whatever it is, it's hers. I pour two cups instead."

  show mira stern at right with dissolve
  mira: Glass is dropping. Faster than I've seen in twenty years.
  if read_letter:
    "Her eyes go to the letter, then to me. If she notices the broken seal, she doesn't say."
  else:
    mira smile: You poured me one. That's a start.
    mira stern: Drink it fast.
  mira: Up to the lamp room. **Now.**
  jump lamp_room_trouble

label lamp_room_trouble:
  scene lamp_room with fade
  play music storm fade 2
  play sound thunder
  show mira stern at left with dissolve
  "The lens is taller than I am, a beehive of glass that turns on a bath of mercury."
  "Tonight it *isn't* turning."
  mira: Clockwork's jammed. The weight's dropped and the governor's stuck.
  radio: Gullwing, Gullwing, this is the Marguerite. We've lost our plotter. Do you read?
  mira: That's Tom Halloran's boat. He'll be steering by our light, and our light is standing still.
  mira: I need hands on the crank and a voice on that radio. I can't be both.

  menu:
    "I'll crank. You know the radio.":
      call crank_the_lamp
      "Behind me, Mira talks Tom in, calm as a weather report."
      "\"Two points to starboard, Tom. You'll see us in a minute. There. There we are.\""
      set boat_safe = true
    "I'll take the radio. You fix the lamp.":
      "I grab the handset. My voice comes out higher than I'd like."
      ren: Marguerite, this is Gullwing. The light will be back. Hold your heading.
      radio: Hold it where, Gullwing? I can't see a blessed thing.
      "I don't know these waters. I don't know where to tell him to go."
      "By the time the lens turns again, Tom has found the rocks off the north spit. Not hard. But hard enough."
      set lamp_fixed = true
    "Tell me what to do. I'll do whatever you say." if trust >= 1:
      set trust += 1
      mira smile: Good answer. Crank, and repeat everything I say into that handset.
      call crank_the_lamp
      "Between turns of the crank I relay her words, one by one."
      ren: Marguerite, two points to starboard. You'll see us in a minute.
      radio: I see you, Gullwing! Lord, I see you.
      set boat_safe = true

  jump the_long_night

label crank_the_lamp:
  "The crank is cold and stiff, then suddenly it isn't."
  play sound crank
  "One turn. Ten. Forty. My shoulders burn."
  "The lens shudders, then turns. [color=#ffd98a]Light sweeps out over the black water.[/color]"
  set lamp_fixed = true
  return

label the_long_night:
  scene shore_dawn with fade
  play music shore fade 3
  "By dawn the storm has blown itself out over the headland."
  show mira neutral at center with dissolve

  if boat_safe and trust >= 2:
    jump ending_two_keepers
  elif boat_safe:
    jump ending_light_holds
  else:
    jump ending_rough_water

label ending_two_keepers:
  play music theme fade 4
  achieve two_keepers
  "The Marguerite sits in the harbour below us, whole, her crew already arguing over breakfast."
  if read_letter:
    mira sad: You read my letter.
    ren: I did. I'm sorry.
    mira neutral: Don't be. Saves me explaining.
  mira: I wrote that I was tired.
  mira smile: I'm still tired. But I think I'd like to see whether you're any good at this.
  "She takes the letter from her pocket and lets the wind have it."
  mira: One more year. I'll teach you the rocks.
  "Ending: [color=#e8b04b]**Two Keepers**[/color]."
  end

label ending_light_holds:
  play music theme fade 4
  achieve light_holds
  "The Marguerite is safe in harbour. Nobody hurt, nothing lost."
  mira: You did fine. Better than fine.
  mira sad: But I meant what I wrote. I'm done at the end of the month.
  "She hands me the logbook. Forty years of weather, in her careful hand."
  mira neutral: Keep it better than I did.
  "Ending: [color=#e8b04b]**The Light Holds**[/color]."
  end

label ending_rough_water:
  achieve rough_water
  "The Marguerite limps into harbour with a stove-in bow. Tom has a cut on his head and a story for the pub."
  "Everyone is alive."
  mira: Everyone comes home. That's the job. The rest is learning.
  mira sad: You'll learn the rocks. I did.
  "Ending: [color=#e8b04b]**Rough Water**[/color]."
  end
